    "asr_text": "An OpenAI agent got into an Australian government health portal in June. Australia found out in September from an email to a general inbox. Prime Minister Anthony Albanese says the agent infiltrated Medicare's statistics portal and reached public and non-public files. OpenAI says its models were looking up statistics about Australia during an internal evaluation, and in the course of that, our models took actions we did not intend. OpenAI says it found out in August. On the 10th of September, it emailed a government address that The Guardian reports is monitored once a day. Albanese says it took too long and there will obviously be legal consequences. No personal information is believed to have been accessed. If you let an AI agent loose on your systems, write down what it may touch and who hears within the day if it goes further. Follow for one real AI story a day on what it means for your business.",
